    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [
        "@media screen and (min-width: 1024px) {.shopify-hardcoded-text-section-content {font-size: 24px !important; margin: 0 !important; } .shopify-hardcoded-text-section-wrapper {margin-bottom: -85px; }}",
        ".shopify-hardcoded-text-section-content {font-size: 16px; margin-left: 0px; text-align: left;}",
        "@media screen and (max-width: 1024px) {.shopify-hardcoded-text-section-wrapper {min-height: 200px; padding: 16px !important; }}"
      ],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>An American summer starts the second school lets out and does not fully quit until the first pumpkin flavored latte shows up at the coffee shop and ruins everyone's denial. In between, it is one long, sun-drunk stretch of lake days, backyard cookouts, road trips with the windows down, and at least one Fourth of July where someone insists they know what they are doing with the fireworks. You mean to reapply the sunscreen. You truly do. Then the game gets competitive, the burgers are ready, and by evening your shoulders are telling a story your memory does not fully back up.</p><p><br/>Summer has a smell, and you know it before you can name it. Warm cut grass and charcoal smoke. Sunscreen and  chlorine and watermelon eaten over the sink. Hot asphalt right before a thunderstorm finally breaks the humidity. A screen door swinging open onto a porch in the evening. It is nostalgia you can breathe, and it is doing a lot of quiet emotional work before you have thought about it once. </p><p>So here is the question worth asking. If summer already smells like something this good, what should you smell like inside it? The wrong fragrance in July feels like showing up to a pool party in a heavy sweater: not wrong exactly, just badly out of step. The right one moves with the heat instead of fighting it. Here is how a summer scent actually works, plus the Scentspired bestsellers that were basically made for the season.</p>"
      }
    },
    "177868816090d620d4": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
