        "ai_gen_block_fb81b45_9nTtAA",
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_zVYidR"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_jgTJWD": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_19f144a",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "Timeless Grace",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 300,
            "line_2_text": "vs",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "Coco Mademoiselle by Chanel:",
            "line_3_alignment": "right",
            "line_3_offset": -40,
            "body_text": "<p>Coco Mademoiselle is the benchmark for a certain kind of feminine fragrance. Clean, grown-up, and immediately recognisable. It has been the top-selling women's perfume in the UK and US for years. The EDP retails at around $160 for 100ml and it earns that position consistently.</p><p><strong>Timeless Grace</strong> opens with the same fresh orange and bergamot, develops through jasmine and rose, and settles into a warm patchouli base that wears throughout the day. The comparison test here produced the closest result of the three: on dry-down, both fragrances sat in the same warm, clean territory. The original has a very slight additional depth in the base that reflects the higher concentration of raw materials, but it is a difference you would only notice if you were specifically looking for it.<br/><br/>At around $20 versus $160, Timeless Grace makes a compelling case for anyone who loves the Coco Mademoiselle profile but wants to wear it every day without the creeping sense that they should be saving it for something more significant.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 44,
            "line_2_size": 85,
            "line_3_size": 44,
            "body_size": 22,
            "line_2_margin_top": 30,
            "line_3_margin_top": 4,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 1000,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#121212"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_kVmwE7"
      ],
      "name": "Staggered typography",
      "settings": {}
    },
    "17786893180b60ea14": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_c88e324",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "container_width": 1200,
            "left_column_width": 40,
            "right_column_width": 60,
            "column_gap": 40,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "heading": "Where The Differences actually Show Up",
            "heading_font": "serif",
            "heading_size": 56,
            "mobile_heading_size": 40,
            "heading_color": "#000000",
            "heading_indent": 10,
            "mobile_heading_indent": 40,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/magnific_luxury-perfume-comparison_74h5S6MJAL_jpg.jpg",
            "image_max_width": 600,
            "heading_image_gap": 4,
            "mobile_heading_image_gap": 25,
            "body_text": "<p>Across all our tests, the differences between inspired fragrances and originals came down to three things.<br/><br/><strong>Concentration of raw materials</strong>. Designer houses use extremely high concentrations of expensive ingredients. The originals have a certain richness in the base that reflects this. A well-made inspired fragrance gets close, but the very finest nuances of a $300 bottle are sometimes in those base notes, and it is worth knowing that going in.<br/><br/><strong>Projection in the opening</strong>. Top notes on the originals tend to radiate a little further, particularly in the first half an hour after applying. This matters if you are spraying in an elevator and want to make an immediate impression. It matters less if you are wearing something all day for yourself.<br/><br/><strong>Longevity on dry skin</strong>. Both perform significantly better on moisturised skin. On dry skin, the originals do have a slight edge in staying power. The fix is twelve seconds of moisturiser before you spray. After that, the gap closes considerably.</p>",
            "body_font": "system_ui_n4",
            "body_size": 24,
            "mobile_body_size": 16,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 30,
            "mobile_paragraph_spacing": 15,
            "text_vertical_offset": 10,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "padding_top": 100,
            "padding_bottom": 100,
            "horizontal_padding": 40,
            "mobile_padding_top": 60,
            "mobile_padding_bottom": 60,
            "mobile_horizontal_padding": 20,
            "mobile_gap": 30
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "ai_gen_block_c88e324_m8PFU4"
      ],
      "settings": {}
    },
    "blocks_g6VtBW": {
      "type": "_blocks",
      "blocks": {
        "ai_gen_block_19f144a_BAgRLn": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_19f144a",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "line_1_text": "The one who is",
            "line_1_alignment": "left",
            "line_1_offset": 155,
            "line_2_text": "nearly impossible",
            "line_2_alignment": "center",
            "line_2_offset": 0,
            "line_3_text": "to shop for",
            "line_3_alignment": "center",
            "line_3_offset": 200,
            "body_text": "<p>Every friend group has one person who is nearly impossible to shop for. They already own what they want, care more about quality than quantity, and will<br/>absolutely return whatever misses. A unisex fragrance is the smartest move here, since it skips the guesswork of gendered marketing altogether. Cool Alpine, inspired by Silver Mountain Water by Creed, is clean and universally flattering enough that it rarely misses, whoever ends up opening it, which makes it the closest thing to a safe pick that still feels like an actual gift instead of a placeholder.</p>",
            "line_1_size": 40,
            "line_2_size": 55,
            "line_3_size": 40,
            "body_size": 22,
            "line_2_margin_top": 40,
            "line_3_margin_top": -14,
            "header_spacing": 40,
            "body_max_width": 900,
            "section_padding_top": 60,
            "section_padding_bottom": 60,
            "background_color": "#ffffff",
            "text_color": "#000000"
          },
          "blocks": {}
        },
        "ai_gen_block_614820f_AUBiD6": {
          "type": "ai_gen_block_614820f",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Luminous Wonder (inspired by J'Adore by Dior): sunshine, bottled",
            "heading_size": 50,
            "heading_size_mobile": 32,
            "heading_line_height": 1,
            "heading_color": "#121212",
            "heading_margin_bottom": 50,
            "heading_margin_bottom_mobile": 30,
            "column_1_text": "<p>A lot of florals save themselves for cooler weather. Luminous Wonder does its best work in the sun. Inspired by J'Adore, it is a glowing bouquet of ylang-ylang, rose, and jasmine that stays golden instead of tipping into heavy, which is not an easy thing for a floral to pull off once it warms up. It smells like the best part of summer: warm skin, a garden at full tilt, that flash of feeling completely put together.</p>",
            "column_2_text": "<p>This is a <a href=\"/collections/women\" title=\"Women\">best perfume for women</a> who want something unmistakably feminine and celebratory that will not turn cloying by mid-afternoon. It carries beautifully in warm air, so a light hand does the job. Wear it to anything worth putting on a nice dress for, and it will hold right through to the part of the night where someone suggests one more stop.</p>",
            "body_size": 20,
            "body_size_mobile": 14,
            "body_line_height": 1.6,
            "body_color": "#000000",
            "paragraph_spacing": 20,
            "column_gap": 60,
            "column_gap_mobile": 30,
            "max_width": 1000,
            "desktop_width_percent": 100,
            "background_color": "#f9f6f1",
            "padding_top": 60,
            "padding_bottom": 60,
            "padding_horizontal": 40,
            "padding_top_mobile": 40,
            "padding_bottom_mobile": 40,
            "padding_horizontal_mobile": 20
          },
          "blocks": {}
        }
      },
